# @repo/access

One place for what every LogueBio tool needs to adapt to the person using it:

- **Settings** (`useAccess`, `updateSettings`, `AccessSettingsPanel`): colour scheme,
  contrast, colour-blind palette, text size and spacing, motion, autoplay, simpler
  interface, reading time, explanations, sound and vibration. Saved in a cookie that
  every tool shares (localhost ports share cookies in development; `.loguebio.com`
  in production), with a localStorage copy. Nothing leaves the device.
- **What the person declares wins**: `resolveSettings` only falls back to the
  device's own settings (reduced motion, dark mode) when the choice is "Follow my device".
- **Palette** (`categoryColors`, `cividis`): Okabe-Ito categories, a blue-yellow
  (tritan) set and a high-contrast set, in one fixed order; cividis for scales.
  Always pair colour with a shape or a word.
- **Announcer** (`announce`): hidden live regions; drops repeats, merges polite
  messages by `topic`, and spaces them out (`setAnnounceGap`, longer with
  "longer reading time").
- **Vibration** (`canVibrate`, `vibrate`): only when turned on and supported.

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx: apply saved settings before first paint
import { ACCESS_BOOT_SCRIPT } from '@repo/access/boot';   // server-safe entry
<head><script dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: ACCESS_BOOT_SCRIPT }} /></head>

// any client component
'use client';
import { useAccess, applySettingsToDocument, AccessSettingsPanel, announce } from '@repo/access';
const access = useAccess();
useEffect(() => applySettingsToDocument(access), [access]);
announce('3 droplets formed', { topic: 'droplets' });
```

The `<html>` element then carries `data-theme`, `data-contrast`, `data-motion`,
`data-spacing`, `data-palette`, `data-simpler` and `data-text-size` (100, 125,
150, 200), and `--access-text-scale` for CSS. Screen-width media queries ignore
the text size, so use `data-text-size` to drop columns when text is large.

Plain JavaScript with type declarations, like `@repo/suite`, so it needs no build
step and no `transpilePackages`.
